<title>UK: Breakdown of shareholders in Ivory &amp; Sime.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of shareholders in Ivory &amp; Sime.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>According to the 1996 annual report, the following substantial interests were identified in the Scottish fund management group Ivory &amp; Sime, whose managing director Colin Hook quit on Monday.</p>
<p>							Shares     Percentage</p>
<p>    Caledonia Investments plc		 9,250,610     29.1</p>
<p>    Sumitomo Life Insurance Co		4,358,333     13.7</p>
<p>    Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co	     1,315,000     4.1</p>
<p>    Acorn International Fund		  1,280,000     4.0</p>
<p>    I F Rushbrook				 1,200,000     3.8</p>
<p>    Bank of England Pension Fund	    1,145,000     3.3</p>
<p>* The Ivory &amp; Sime Retirement and Death Benefits plan owns all of the 17.5 percent Cumulative Preference Share Capital. The accounts reported a 39 percent increase in funds under management to 4.3 billion stg for 1996 to April 30. Profits before tax rose by 10 percent to 6.5 million stg, earnings per share were at 13.71 p compared to 12.95 and total dividends rose by 10 percent to 8.25p/share for the full year.</p>
<p>Caledonia Investments is a holding company controlled by the Cayzer family whose investment roots are in its shipping empire.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6414</p>
